        "text": "Wrote `verdicts-1.jsonl` (150 lines, one per packet line) and `node check.mjs 1` passes: 150 judged, 103 accepted, 47 rejected, no format problems.\n\n**How the rejections break down**\n\n| Grade | Count | Pattern that triggered it |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| L1 | 15 | command written as a clause of another form, an auxiliary or direction word made the verb, a command's verb held as a noun/dependent |\n| L3 | 27 | a word after a measure or of place/order held as a nominal dependent, linking words (`of`, `for`, `to`, `also`, `not`) inside a nominal, merged or split nominals |\n| L5 | 3 | a whole instruction whose verb survives only as a modifier, dependent or head |\n| L2 | 1 | `ahve` (a missed `have`) put in `discourse`, so the `have … stay` command vanishes |\n| L4 | 1 | `make the bars blue` given an invented subject from an earlier list |\n\n**Judgment choices you may want to look at.** Where several grades applied I took the first listed in RULES.md, which is why a verb held as a dependent is sometimes L1 (`change`, `label`, `rotate`, per the settled \"a command needs its verb\" case) and sometimes L5 (`halve`, `est`, `clear`, where the word is not a noun/verb pivot). The narrowest calls are n=57 (`of` as a bare modifier in a garbled chart phrase), n=62 (`to` as a dependent of `15`), n=127 (`also` as a dependent of `Sales`), n=146 (`Deep Dive left Summary` merged) and n=41 (`Let us` written interrogative) — each quotes the words and names a concrete wrong statement, but each is one step from a pass. Garbled or truncated messages where every word is placed and tied (4, 38, 63, 68, 75, 81, 109, 116, 124) I accepted, relying on the misspelt/unknown-word and noun-or-verb tolerances.\n\nNo other file was touched; the generator script lived in `/tmp`."
      }
